# Rottenmouth Viper's punishment: each opponent makes all of their choices, one for each blight counter, and then the
# actions happen together (the rulings, CR 101.4). Bot2 controls Marauding Mako ("whenever you discard one or more cards,
# put that many +1/+1 counters on this creature"). On turn 3 the Viper attacks with its second counter, and Bot2 chooses
# to discard twice: both Lightning Bolts are discarded at once, so the Mako triggers once, for two counters - not once for
# each. (On turn 1, entering, the Viper's one counter cost Bot2 4 life.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Rottenmouth Viper
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Marauding Mako
Lightning Bolt x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Rottenmouth Viper)
Bot2.Choose()
Bot2.Modes(Lose 4 life)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Marauding Mako.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Rottenmouth Viper > Bot2)
Bot2.Modes(Discard a card)
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
Bot2.Modes(Discard a card)
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Battlefield.Marauding Mako.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Life = 10
